  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Core pipeline",
      "items": [
        "6-crate workspace at v1.3.1, edition 2024; SemVer covers commands, flags, MCP tools and schemas",
        "hwp5 and hwpx never depend on each other: both go through the hwp-model IR",
        "Unedited hwp-origin files re-serialize byte-identically (decompressed streams); edited or hwpx/markdown input is rewritten semantically equivalent",
        "Codecs open inputs by path; command outputs and hwp_put_file are staged, verified, renamed; serve /files writes in place"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Formats and forms",
      "items": [
        "cat: plain/markdown/JSON/HTML/CSV; convert to hwp, hwpx, md, json, html, pdf, odt, txt, csv, docx",
        "hwp-render draws PNG/SVG/PDF; the command layer encodes JPEG/WebP from the raster; render-layout-v1 rows include drawing-object text",
        "slots --forms and fill --forms: Korean form fields (label cells, label: value, blanks, checkboxes)",
        "lint: 10 rule ids; 6 official-document profiles"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "MCP and deployment",
      "items": [
        "22 tools reuse the command modules' execute and publish helpers (not their stdout run paths); stdio and HTTP share one handle_request core",
        "hwp serve: close-per-request POST /mcp on httparse, 1 MiB body cap, private hop behind a trusted edge",
        "hwp mcp without --root is unrestricted (warns); hwp serve always requires --root",
        "Tier A Cloudflare (OAuth or PAT, /files sideband) and Tier B AgentCore (/mcp only) images pin v1.3.1"
      ]
    }
  ]
